  "notes": [
   "The catalogue entry for arduino-leonardo lists no ports; port names used (5V, GND.1, GND.2, A0, A1, 5, 6) follow the Uno naming and the labels in the circuit image.",
   "Joystick module sits in breadboard column 12 (rows j..f, VCC/VERT/HORZ/SEL/GND). Jumper wires land in column 11, same rows. The image's top half is rows f-j, so it is bank 'b' in the catalogue naming.",
   "Wire colours/mapping from the image: red 5V->VCC, yellow A0->VERT, green A1->HORZ, blue D6->SEL, black GND->GND. This matches the schematic.",
   "The optional status LED on pin 5 (with 220 ohm series resistor) is included. Its placement on the breadboard (columns 20-24, bank 't') is my assumption, since the manual only refers to the Blink circuit. The LED ground wire goes to the Leonardo's second GND pin.",
   "The optional second pushbutton on D3 with a 10k pulldown is not built because the manual says it is only 'if needed' and gives no layout. The joystick's SEL button is wired to pin 6 with no external pulldown.",
   "The USB cable to the computer is mentioned in the text but not drawn, so it is not included."
  ]
